1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,620
Across Pluto's horizon,

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:04,140
what would you see on the bright western

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:05,900
half of its icy heart?

4
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:08,580
A frozen nitrogen glacier

5
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:11,160
about 1,000 kilometers wide,

6
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:14,100
larger than Texas and Oklahoma combined,

7
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:16,240
with zero craters.

8
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:20,240
On 13th and 14th July 2015,

9
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:22,940
NASA's New Horizons spacecraft

10
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:26,900
flew within 12,500 kilometers of Pluto,

11
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:30,460
39 times farther from the Sun than Earth,

12
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:34,120
at minus 232 degrees Celsius,

13
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:36,020
and solved that mystery.
